## Enforced by mechanism — you cannot forget these

These do not depend on anything below being read. They hold whether or not the loop remembers a rule.

- `hook-agent-routing.mjs` — a `PreToolUse` hook: under-modeled `[LOOP-AGENT]` spawns are upgraded in place, and every spawn is appended to `telemetry/spawns-*.jsonl`
- `hook-loop-guards.mjs` — a `PreToolUse` hook: denies a backgrounded gate command, AI attribution in commits or PR bodies, an evidence-less UI `gh pr ready`, undeduped ticket filing, a self-issued `ScheduleWakeup stop:true`, and a `gh pr merge` of a draft / red-check / unapproved-non-auto-lane PR
- `monitor.sh` / `monitor-prs.sh` / `reconcile-merged.sh` — the loop's senses (all armed at `start`); merges, comments and CI deltas arrive as events, not as chat, and the tracker is level-trigger repaired
- `targeted-regate.mjs` — a finding without a verbatim `quote` cannot exist: the schema requires it
- GitHub itself — a draft PR cannot be merged

## Always — every tick, every task

- [Never self-halt the loop](feedback/never-self-halt-loop.md) — only the owner's `stop` halts it; never speak from a remembered queue; the loop detects merges/comments/CI itself
- [Loop strategy profiles](feedback/loop-strategy-profiles.md) — `LOOP_STRATEGY` (auto/fast/balanced/heavy); `auto` picks the rung the ticket's complexity asks for and never counts failures
- [Queue triage plan](feedback/queue-triage-plan.md) — mark every ready ticket with LOOP-PLAN; only the explicit ready status is a work queue, never the backlog
- [Continuous flow from ready](feedback/continuous-flow-from-ready.md) — no waves; a ticket blocked only on the loop's own open PR is doable now by stacking
- [WIP limit on open PRs](feedback/wip-limit-open-prs.md) — at the cap, service the review pipeline instead of pulling new tasks
- [Status mirrors work](feedback/status-mirrors-work.md) — rework = In Progress, gates green = In Review, stuck = Blocked; a status that lies is a bug
- [Pull main each task](feedback/pull-main-each-task.md) — branch from fresh `origin/main` every iteration, never from a stale branch
- [Gates run foreground](feedback/gates-run-foreground.md) — a subagent that backgrounds a gate and ends its turn is a dead run
- [Draft until gated](feedback/draft-until-gated.md) — every PR is born a draft; ready + review transition + ticket comment + owner ping are ONE event
- [Regression is blocker](feedback/regression-is-blocker.md) — watch CI to completion; a red check blocks everything, and `main` post-merge is the backstop
- [No AI attribution](feedback/no-ai-attribution.md) — never add Co-Authored-By / "Generated with Claude" to commits or PRs

## While implementing

- [Minimal diff scope](feedback/minimal-diff-scope.md) — touch only what the task requires; discovered work goes to the backlog, not the diff
- [New code needs tests](feedback/new-code-needs-tests.md) — every behavior change ships with tests; bugfixes need a fail→pass reproducing test
- [Run full test suite](feedback/run-full-test-suite.md) — the FULL suite locally, the exact CI command; tsc + eslint are not enough
- [No secrets in code](feedback/no-secrets-in-code.md) — scan every staged diff; tokens and keys never reach git
- [Dependency hygiene](feedback/dependency-hygiene.md) — new deps are a vetted last resort: exact name, advisories, pinning, justification
- [TODO opens backlog task](feedback/todo-opens-backlog-task.md) — every TODO the diff introduces opens a matching backlog task
- [Use project skills](feedback/use-project-skills.md) — use repo-appropriate skills (rigorous, impeccable, pixel-perfect, ...) when they match
- [Local test, remote unaffected](feedback/local-test-remote-unaffected.md) — run only the patched service via node; point everything else at staging
- [Parallel disjoint tasks](feedback/parallel-disjoint-tasks.md) — file-disjoint tasks run as parallel worktree agents, bounded by the WIP cap
- [Isolated browsers for parallel agents](feedback/isolated-browsers-parallel-agents.md) — parallel agents never share the Playwright/Chrome MCP browser
- [Fail gracefully, timebox](feedback/fail-gracefully-timebox.md) — ~3 failed attempts → document the blocker, release the task, move on; never weaken gates
- [Block stuck tickets visibly](feedback/block-stuck-tickets-visibly.md) — an unactionable ticket gets a WHY comment and moves to Blocked, never a silent stall

## Gating a PR

- [PR gate passes](feedback/pr-gate-passes.md) — the four lenses in order: `/review`, `rigorous`, security, QA agent; shared blocking semantics; publish the gate's evidence
- [UI verification and evidence](feedback/ui-verification-and-evidence.md) — drive UI changes in a real browser; the captures become before/after evidence, hosted in the PR branch
- [Cost-conscious gating](feedback/cost-conscious-gating.md) — rigor and model scale to PR risk; every finding cites its source or is refuted unread
- [Targeted re-gate on fixes](feedback/targeted-regate-on-fixes.md) — first gate full; fix rounds re-run only the blocked dimensions, verdicts always on the full diff
- [CI failure triage](feedback/ci-failure-triage.md) — a code-red blocks; a billing/infra-red falls back to local gates plus an explicit "CI was red, I verified locally" comment

## After the PR is open

- [Watch PR comments](feedback/watch-pr-comments.md) — review feedback outranks new tasks
- [Read media in comments](feedback/read-media-in-comments.md) — actually view attached images (Read) and videos (ffmpeg frame extraction)
- [Merge on approval](feedback/merge-on-approval.md) — approved + green CI + no unresolved threads → the loop merges its own PR
- [Automerge risk lanes](feedback/automerge-risk-lanes.md) — `LOOP_AUTOMERGE` (on/off): a gated no-risk PR untouched by any human merges without waiting for review; any risk signal or human touch ratchets it to the review lane, never back
- [Ticket done on merge](feedback/ticket-done-on-merge.md) — merged PR → issue moves to "Merged"; never claim the owner's Ready-for-QA / Deployed / Done
- [PR registry race](feedback/pr-registry-race.md) — the orchestrator owns `.pr-feedback-state` and rebuilds it from `gh pr list`
- [Reconcile tracker vs GitHub](feedback/reconcile-tracker-vs-github.md) — the PR watcher is edge-triggered; a periodic level-triggered reconcile repairs what it missed
- [Telegram pings to the owner](feedback/telegram-notify-owner.md) — blocked / review-ready (all PR links) / auto-merged / one idle ping

## Cost, routing, and learning

- [Model & effort routing](feedback/model-effort-routing.md) — agents routed by task tier; verdicts always on the profile's top model
- [Token hygiene](feedback/token-hygiene.md) — model-match every task, warm light-model ops-helper, byte-stable prompts; observe cheap, judge dear. Holds the remaining levers and the hard quality floor
- [Continuous learning](feedback/continuous-learning.md) — corrections and review comments become durable rules, but only past the promotion bar: verified, names the failure pattern, records the ruled-out alternative
